# The pixel oracles, pinned.
#
# One line per reference, tab-separated: <name> <image> <version> <what it
# answers>. Machine-read by tools/oracle/oracle_env.py.
#
# Built here: no upstream digest of the finished image. What is pinned is
# everything the Containerfile reads, and the run-time version check is the
# guarantee. Raising a pin is deliberate: a newer renderer is newer answers.
#
# Building them:
#   make oracle-images

# resvg 0.45.1 (Debian). Renders an SVG file to a PNG of a stated size.
resvg	localhost/ghoti-vector-oracle-resvg:0.45.1	resvg 0.45.1	SVG to PNG; the renderer the test suite's references were made and reviewed against

# Inkscape 1.4 (Debian). Renders an SVG file to a PNG of a stated size,
# headless.
inkscape	localhost/ghoti-vector-oracle-inkscape:1.4	Inkscape 1.4	SVG to PNG by an independent renderer

# Chrome for Testing 156 (Blink) and Firefox 158 (Gecko), with the drivers that read `getComputedStyle()` of an SVG document. The style
# oracle compares the computed values of this library with what both browsers say.
browser	localhost/ghoti-vector-oracle-browser:156.0.8078.47-158.0.1	chrome 156.0.8078.47	computed style of an SVG document, from two independent engines
